MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles and the Beach Boys feel like natural next choices because I want familiar older rock and melodic pop, much like my Beatles and mid-sixties collections.",
    "The Best of Bread fits the mellow listening mood suggested by Simon & Garfunkel and Jonathan Edwards; that connection matters more to me than simply being a hits collection."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "25, In The Lonely Hour, and Adele 21 do not connect as closely to the older rock and folk songs I want right now, even though I have listened to newer music before.",
    "Partners and Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 and 2 leave me unsure what music I would get; I cannot choose them confidently without knowing the artist or songs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My occasional interest in newer pop seems to have been taken as a stronger guide to my current mood than it is.",
    "A greatest-hits label alone is not enough: the artist, era, and sound determine whether a collection appeals to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of older-song collections, including the Melanie compilation, suggest that familiar older music remains a strong draw for me.",
    "There is a difference between something I might enjoy and something I would choose now: Earth Wind & Fire and the Guardians collection appeal to me, but Eagles, the Beach Boys, and Bread fit my mood more closely."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in older hits, but gave too much weight to broader pop interest and too little to the particular artists and sounds I want now."
}
